 25	 * other, numbers, dates and any figure a statement bound kept, listed after the other's own in the
 26	 * order they were added. Their name and aliases become aliases of the other; their
 27	 * patrons are added to the other's (not the other themselves, no repeats); anyone naming them as a
 28	 * patron names the other instead (no repeats); their pool memberships move to the other, shares added
 29	 * where the other is already a member; the crews they lead are led by the other and their crew
 30	 * memberships move to the other, dropped where the other is in the crew already; their plans become the other's. Their statements join the
 31	 * other's: the other's count becomes their own plus theirs, and the other's last statement stays the
 32	 * other's (or, the other having none, becomes theirs). Their holds, watchers and contact are dropped,
 33	 * and they leave the sheet, kept aside so the merge can be undone.
 34	 * <p>
 35	 * The last merge into a person can be undone by the steward who made it, on the same sheet-today: the
 36	 * merged person is back at the end of the list with the claims that came from them (as they are now)
 37	 * and their own name and aliases, which the other no longer goes by. Patron, pool, crew, plan and
 38	 * statement changes stay.
